From 1000000000000000000000000000000000000474 Tue Sep  1 00:00:00 2026
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:24:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: bind Gemini CPU9 progress configuration

The bounded progress diagnostic changes the exact ordered production
configuration inputs from cda6d936... to c10a2188.... Bind the MT6797
production profile to that package-derived identity so its existing preflight
can distinguish this diagnostic from the retired CPU9 controller candidate.

Keep the fixture identity unchanged and add no CPU request, retained write,
power, retry, CPU_OFF, storage, or device action.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
index 5cac538..8f90ee7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
@@ -64,8 +64,8 @@ static const u64 mt6797_a72_config_input_identity[ARM64_LATE_CPU_ID_WORDS] __ini
 };
 #else
 static const u64 mt6797_a72_config_input_identity[ARM64_LATE_CPU_ID_WORDS] __initconst = {
-	0xcda6d936e61122d8, 0x25a7fe7649f1b69b,
-	0x86455d6034f36a6c, 0xd562ff457bccd3d1,
+	0xc10a21881871dd9a, 0xad61f259d660a62f,
+	0xc24f989cb165bb61, 0xdc53af45438fe898,
 };
 #endif
 
